   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law and the village law, in relation to\nresidency requirements for the village clerk/treasurer and the deputy clerk\nfor the village of Cold Spring",
    "basePrintNo": "S7434",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7434-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L; amd §3-300, Vil L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7434\n\nSPONSOR: ROLISON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law and the village law, in relation\nto residency requirements for the village clerk/treasurer and the deputy\nclerk for the village of Cold Spring\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to waive the residency requirements\nfor the village clerk/treasurer and the deputy clerk for the village of\nCold Spring.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends Section 3 of the Public Officers Law by adding a new\nsubdivision 73 that allows a person holding the office of village\nclerk/treasurer and the deputy clerk of the village of cold spring to\nreside within the state of New York.\n\nSection 2. Amends Section 3-300 of the Village Law by adding a new\nsection 33 allowing the Village Board of Trustees of the Incorporated\nVillage of Cold Spring, County of Putnam, may, by resolution, provide\nthat the village clerk/treasurer and the deputy clerk of the village of\nCold Spring, Putnam County, need not be a resident of Cold Spring as\nlong as they are a resident of New York State.\n\nSection 3. Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is necessary to ensure that the Village of Cold Spring\ncan draw from a pool of the most qualified individuals for the important\nfunctions of Village Clerk - Treasurer and Deputy Clerk and not from a\npool based on geographic qualifications.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
